The partial document outlines a series of error codes (E10034 to E10041) related to invalid arguments in the CANN (Compute Architecture for Neural Networks) community edition, specifically during model conversion or configuration using the ATC (Ascend Tensor Compiler) tool. It details symptoms and corresponding solutions for each error, focusing on issues such as:  
- Incompatible data types (e.g., FP16 nodes connected to AIPP);  
- Incorrect usage of dynamic shape parameters (--dynamic_batch_size, --dynamic_image_size, --dynamic_dims), including too few or too many profiles, inconsistent dimension counts across profiles, invalid (non-positive) dimension sizes, and duplicate profiles;  
- Mismatches between dynamic shape arguments and input shape specifications (e.g., missing -1 axes or improper use of '~');  
- Failure to load a model file.  
Each entry provides actionable steps to resolve the configuration errors, often involving adjusting command-line arguments or modifying input node definitions.

